sequenceDiagram
    participant BE as Backend Process
    participant CP as CheckpointerMain
    participant WAL as WAL System
    participant BUF as Buffer Manager
    participant CTL as Control File
    participant DISK as Storage

    Note over BE,DISK: WAL-Checkpoint Coordination Timeline

    %% Initial trigger
    BE->>CP: RequestCheckpoint(flags)
    Note over BE,CP: Trigger: Manual, time-based, or WAL volume

    CP->>CP: Validate checkpoint conditions
    CP->>CP: Initialize checkpoint statistics

    Note over CP,WAL: Phase 1: Establish REDO Point (Critical Section)

    CP->>WAL: START_CRIT_SECTION()
    CP->>WAL: WALInsertLockAcquireExclusive()
    Note over WAL: Block all concurrent WAL insertions

    CP->>WAL: Capture current insertion state
    WAL->>WAL: Determine REDO point LSN
    alt Normal Checkpoint
        CP->>WAL: XLogInsert(RM_XLOG_ID, XLOG_CHECKPOINT_REDO)
        WAL->>WAL: Insert REDO record, assign LSN
        WAL->>DISK: Write REDO record to WAL buffer
    else Restart Point (Recovery)
        CP->>WAL: Use replayed checkpoint REDO point
        Note over WAL: No new WAL record during recovery
    end

    CP->>WAL: Update shared RedoRecPtr
    CP->>WAL: WALInsertLockRelease()
    Note over WAL: Resume concurrent WAL insertions

    CP->>WAL: END_CRIT_SECTION()

    Note over CP,BUF: Phase 2: Transaction Coordination

    CP->>CP: GetVirtualXIDsDelayingChkpt(DELAY_CHKPT_START)
    loop While transactions in commit critical sections
        CP->>CP: AbsorbSyncRequests() - Handle pending fsyncs
        CP->>CP: pg_usleep(10ms) - Brief wait
        CP->>CP: Check if transactions finished critical sections
    end

    Note over CP,DISK: Phase 3: Buffer Synchronization with WAL Coordination

    CP->>BUF: CheckPointBuffers() → BufferSync()

    BUF->>BUF: Scan and mark dirty buffers (BM_CHECKPOINT_NEEDED)
    BUF->>BUF: Sort buffers by tablespace for optimal I/O

    loop For each dirty buffer (tablespace balanced)
        BUF->>BUF: SyncOneBuffer() - Process individual buffer

        Note over BUF,DISK: Per-Buffer WAL-Before-Data Enforcement
        BUF->>BUF: Get buffer LSN (PageLSN)
        BUF->>WAL: XLogFlush(buffer_lsn) - Ensure WAL before data

        alt WAL needs flushing
            WAL->>WAL: Acquire WALWriteLock (exclusive)
            WAL->>WAL: WaitXLogInsertionsToFinish() - Coordination point

            Note over WAL,DISK: Group Commit Optimization
            WAL->>WAL: Collect additional flush requests
            alt CommitDelay > 0 and sufficient backends
                WAL->>WAL: pg_usleep(CommitDelay) - Allow batching
                WAL->>WAL: Extend flush target for group commit
            end

            WAL->>DISK: XLogWrite() - Physical WAL I/O
            DISK->>DISK: Write WAL pages to disk
            alt End of WAL segment
                DISK->>DISK: issue_xlog_fsync() - Force to storage
                WAL->>WAL: Check if checkpoint needed (WAL volume)
                alt WAL volume threshold exceeded
                    WAL->>CP: RequestCheckpoint(CHECKPOINT_CAUSE_XLOG)
                    Note over WAL,CP: Triggers next checkpoint cycle
                end
            end
            WAL->>WAL: Release WALWriteLock
        end

        WAL-->>BUF: WAL flushed to required LSN

        Note over BUF,DISK: Data Page Write After WAL
        BUF->>BUF: PageSetChecksumCopy() - Calculate page checksum
        BUF->>DISK: smgrwrite() - Write data page
        DISK->>DISK: Write data page to storage
        BUF->>BUF: ScheduleBufferTagForWriteback() - Kernel optimization

        BUF->>CP: CheckpointWriteDelay() - Throttle if needed
        alt On schedule with completion target
            CP->>CP: Sleep briefly to spread I/O load
            CP->>CP: AbsorbSyncRequests() during delay
        end
    end

    BUF->>DISK: IssuePendingWritebacks() - Flush kernel buffers
    BUF-->>CP: All dirty buffers synchronized

    Note over CP,DISK: Phase 4: Sync Request Processing

    CP->>CP: ProcessSyncRequests() - Handle accumulated fsyncs
    loop For each pending sync request
        CP->>DISK: fsync() individual files
        DISK-->>CP: Sync complete
    end

    Note over CP,WAL: Phase 5: Final Transaction Coordination

    CP->>CP: GetVirtualXIDsDelayingChkpt(DELAY_CHKPT_COMPLETE)
    loop While transactions in completion critical sections
        CP->>CP: AbsorbSyncRequests()
        CP->>CP: pg_usleep(10ms)
        CP->>CP: Check transaction completion
    end

    Note over CP,WAL: Phase 6: Checkpoint Completion Record

    CP->>WAL: XLogInsert(RM_XLOG_ID, completion_record_type)
    Note over WAL: XLOG_CHECKPOINT_ONLINE or XLOG_CHECKPOINT_SHUTDOWN
    WAL->>WAL: Insert checkpoint completion record
    WAL->>DISK: Write completion record to WAL

    CP->>WAL: XLogFlush(completion_lsn) - Ensure completion record durable
    WAL->>WAL: Final WAL flush for checkpoint
    WAL->>DISK: Ensure checkpoint metadata on disk

    Note over CP,CTL: Phase 7: Control File Update (Atomic)

    CP->>CTL: LWLockAcquire(ControlFileLock, LW_EXCLUSIVE)
    alt Normal Checkpoint
        CP->>CTL: Set state = DB_SHUTDOWNED (if shutdown)
        CP->>CTL: Update checkPoint = completion_record_lsn
        CP->>CTL: Copy checkpoint record to controlfile
        CP->>CTL: Reset minRecoveryPoint (crash recovery to WAL end)
    else Restart Point
        CP->>CTL: Update checkpoint info if newer
        CP->>CTL: Update minRecoveryPoint for backup consistency
        CP->>CTL: Set DB_SHUTDOWNED_IN_RECOVERY (if shutdown)
    end

    CP->>CTL: UpdateControlFile() - Atomic write + fsync
    CTL->>DISK: Write control file atomically
    DISK->>DISK: fsync control file
    CP->>CTL: LWLockRelease(ControlFileLock)

    Note over CP,DISK: Phase 8: WAL Cleanup and Maintenance

    CP->>WAL: Calculate WAL retention requirements
    CP->>WAL: XLogGetReplicationSlotMinimumLSN()
    CP->>WAL: KeepLogSeg() - Determine segments to keep

    alt Replication slots need invalidation
        CP->>WAL: InvalidateObsoleteReplicationSlots()
        CP->>WAL: Recalculate retention after invalidation
    end

    CP->>DISK: RemoveOldXlogFiles() - Clean up old segments
    DISK->>DISK: Delete/recycle obsolete WAL segments

    CP->>DISK: PreallocXlogFiles() - Prepare new segments
    DISK->>DISK: Create new WAL segment files

    Note over CP,BE: Phase 9: Completion Notification

    CP->>CP: Update checkpoint statistics
    CP->>CP: Signal completion to waiting backends
    CP->>BE: ConditionVariableBroadcast() - Wake waiting processes

    BE->>BE: Checkpoint completion detected
    BE->>BE: Continue normal operations

    Note over CP: Checkpoint cycle complete, return to monitoring state

    %% Error handling paths
    Note over CP,DISK: Error Handling (if any phase fails)
    CP->>CP: Critical section cleanup if needed
    CP->>WAL: Release WAL locks if held
    CP->>BUF: Unpin any pinned buffers
    CP->>CTL: Release control file lock if held
    CP->>BE: Signal checkpoint failure
    CP->>CP: Reset checkpoint state, prepare for retry

    %% Timeline annotations
    Note left of CP: Timeline: seconds to minutes depending on buffer pool size and I/O capacity
    Note left of WAL: WAL flushing dominates checkpoint duration due to WAL-before-data rule
    Note left of BUF: Buffer synchronization is most I/O intensive phase
    Note left of CTL: Control file update is atomic and brief but critical for consistency